Fix GRPO LoRA corruption family: de-alias vLLM hot-load tensors (bug c/d root)
and harden the merged_16bit save path against finite-garbage corruption.

Failure signatures fixed:
1. Rollouts rot coherent -> gibberish -> single-token loops within ~5 steps
   when lora_alpha != lora_rank and real (non-zero) lora_B updates flow;
   |B|max on the TRAINING side grows x s^8 per optimizer step (x256 for s=2).
   Cause: load_lora() shipped LIVE training tensors inside
   LoRARequest(lora_tensors=...). vLLM's LoRAModel.from_lora_tensors stores
   tensor.to(device, dtype), a NO-OP (same storage) when device+dtype match,
   and LoRALayerWeights.optimize() then runs `lora_b *= scaling` IN-PLACE on
   the aliased training weight, once per hot-load (8 generation rounds/step).
   Fix: ship detached clones (a few MB per hot-load).
2. In-training save_pretrained_merged(..., "merged_16bit") with the vLLM
   engine alive emits a model whose LoRA-bearing modules carry finite garbage
   ~1e12+ (observed on o_proj/down_proj) while the checkpoint on disk is
   clean. create_lora_statistics stored LIVE GPU references and _merge_lora
   read them only later, mid-merge, racing the allocator churn.
   Fix: snapshot lora_A/lora_B/magnitude to CPU at capture time, plus a
   magnitude tripwire in _merge_lora (|W_merged| vs |W_base|) because the
   existing isfinite gate cannot catch finite garbage.

Applies after unsloth-zoo-9999-vllm-lora-skip-ref-adapter.patch
(same hunk region in load_lora).

